---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { ECON } from "../consts";
---

<Base
  title="Economy · Meridian"
  description="A live read on the Meridian server economy: the Meridian Economic Index, money supply, trade volume, prices, and player wealth."
  path="/economy"
  analytics
>
<main class="doc">
  <h1>Economy</h1>
  <p class="lead">A live read on the Meridian economy, rebuilt from server data. See the <a href="/faq#economy">FAQ</a> for how the economy works.</p>
  <div class="data-stale" data-stale hidden></div>

  <div class="analytics" data-analytics>
    <section id="state">
      <div class="mei" data-slot="mei" data-code="INSUFFICIENT_DATA">
        <div class="mei-top"><span class="mei-label">Loading&hellip;</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-row" data-slot="econ-stats"></div>
    </section>

    <section id="wealth">
      <h2>Wealth</h2>
      <p class="as-sub">The largest player balances on the server.</p>
      <div data-slot="wealth-table"></div>
    </section>

    <section id="markets">
      <h2>Markets</h2>
      <p class="as-sub">Daily open, high, low, and close per item, from chest-shop sales.</p>
      <div class="candles" data-slot="candles"></div>
    </section>

    <section id="prices">
      <h2>Item prices &amp; volume</h2>
      <p class="as-sub">Medians of active chest-shop prices, not fixed rates, with the 7-day change and 30-day trend.</p>
      <div data-slot="item-table"></div>
      <h3>Volume leaders, last 24h</h3>
      <div data-slot="volume-table"></div>
    </section>

    <section id="flow">
      <h2>How money moves</h2>
      <p class="as-sub">Where currency enters the economy, and where it's permanently removed.</p>
      <div class="flow-grid">
        <div class="flow-col flow-source">
          <h3>Sources</h3>
          <div class="flow-item"><span class="f-lab">Starting balance</span><span class="f-val">{ECON.startingBalance}</span><span class="f-note">once, per new player</span></div>
          <div class="flow-item"><span class="f-lab">Jobs payouts</span><span class="f-val">up to {ECON.jobsDailyCap}</span><span class="f-note">per player, per day, capped</span></div>
          <div class="flow-item"><span class="f-lab">Sell counter</span><span class="f-val">floor price</span><span class="f-note">raw metals &amp; minerals</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="flow-col flow-sink">
          <h3>Sinks</h3>
          <div class="flow-item"><span class="f-lab">Land claims</span><span class="f-val">{ECON.firstPaidChunk} +{ECON.chunkIncrease}/chunk</span><span class="f-note">first paid chunk, then rising</span></div>
          <div class="flow-item"><span class="f-lab">Land upkeep</span><span class="f-val">{ECON.landUpkeepPerChunk}/chunk</span><span class="f-note">weekly, per claimed chunk</span></div>
          <div class="flow-item"><span class="f-lab">Nation founding</span><span class="f-val">{ECON.nationCreateCost}</span><span class="f-note">once</span></div>
          <div class="flow-item"><span class="f-lab">Nation upkeep</span><span class="f-val">{ECON.nationUpkeepPerChunk}/chunk</span><span class="f-note">weekly, across all member lands</span></div>
          <div class="flow-item"><span class="f-lab">Buy counter</span><span class="f-val">premium price</span><span class="f-note">essentials, End-exclusives, trims, rare ingredients</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="money">
      <h2>Money &amp; trade</h2>
      <p class="as-sub">Player-held currency, the price index, and daily trade activity.</p>
      <div class="chart-grid">
        <div class="chart">
          <h3>Money supply</h3>
          <div class="c-sub">Total currency held by players.</div>
          <div data-slot="supply-chart"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="chart">
          <h3>Price index</h3>
          <div class="c-sub">Basket of common goods. Base 100 at launch.</div>
          <div data-slot="price-chart"></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="chart">
        <h3>Trade volume</h3>
        <div class="c-sub">Value moving between players and through shops each day.</div>
        <div data-slot="volume-chart"></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <details class="method">
      <summary>How the Meridian Economic Index is calculated</summary>
      <div class="m-body">
        <p>The index reads the server's economy log (every balance change), the land databases, and the shop transaction history. It needs at least <strong>8 active traders</strong> and <strong>14 days</strong> of history before it will assign a state. Each week it compares the last 7 days of trade volume against the 7 days before that:</p>
        <dl>
          <dt>Expansion</dt><dd>Trade volume up more than 10% week over week.</dd>
          <dt>Steady</dt><dd>Trade volume within a &minus;5% to +10% band. A healthy, consistent market.</dd>
          <dt>Cooling</dt><dd>Trade volume down 5% to 25%. Activity is slowing.</dd>
          <dt>Recession</dt><dd>Trade volume down more than 25%, week over week.</dd>
          <dt>Insufficient data</dt><dd>Not enough players or history to judge.</dd>
        </dl>
        <p>The <strong>Gini</strong> figure measures how concentrated wealth is: <code>0</code> means everyone holds the same, <code>1</code> means one player holds everything. The <strong>price index</strong> tracks a fixed basket of wheat, iron, diamonds, ender pearls and oak logs against the median player-shop price for each, set to 100 at launch. Everything on this page refreshes automatically through the day.</p>
      </div>
    </details>
  </div>
</main>
</Base>
